  "text": "4.323% less historical forecast error than Pacific. GPU value scientist shows the evidence. This voice is AI generated. One H100 record stayed at 94 cents per GPU hour while the category median changed. Changing listings can move an index. Our original prediction ranges were too narrow. Human guided calibration widened them without changing the middle. Coverage rose from 64.7 to 75.42%. Later November checks did not confirm the gain. Four agents propose, test, and record forecasting ideas. Later, human guided models failed their checks. Rejections remain visible and our frozen submission stays unchanged. Exa searched inside the loop. Three agents wrote shared pass.dev memory. Two read it. Modal ran eight jobs. Memory matched local accuracy but was slower. White shows recorded prices. Green and gold overlap because our middle prediction matches Pacific. We changed the prediction bounds, not actual prices. Future actual prices are unavailable. For 2029, H100 rents 98 cents to $2.59. A100, 42 cents to $1.20 per GPU hour. Assume scenarios, not tested future prices. After setup, one command rebuilds saved forecasts offline. Sources, frozen protocols, official scores and failures are public. Better historical coverage is measured. A forecasting victory is not proven.",
